  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Checkstyles currently has problems with Java 8 idioms like lambdas and lengthy method call chains. The Maven plugin we use for Checkstyles has been switched off to avoid failing builds in the branch for Java 8 for now:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/tree/Java8"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/tree/Java8",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "but should be fixed and turned back on. Although it would be ideal to actually turn all Checkstyle rules back on, if it is possible to turn on all rules except a small subset that pose difficulties for lamba idioms and the like, that would also be acceptable.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
